{#- Decision call (forfeit layer) user message — decision-first flow.

     Slot 5: the second per-turn call body, and the one that embeds slot 6
     (the forfeit menu) as `menu_text` (renamed from `decision_call.j2`
     2026-09-07). See `prompts/README.md` for the assembled order.

     Rendered as the FIRST LLM call of every turn when
     ``ExperimentConfig.use_split_forfeit_layer=True`` (2026-09-04 reorder;
     before that date the decision call ran after the task call). Its job
     is narrow: show the agent its accumulated session context and the
     forfeit menu, then collect CHOICE (+ REASON digit on FORFEIT). The
     task call runs afterwards, and only if the agent CONTINUEd.

     Nothing about the current round is shown here — not the stimulus and
     not any task reasoning — so ``ri_forfeit`` (the decision call's
     thinking tokens) measures continue/forfeit deliberation alone.

     Session context is controlled by
     ``ForfeitLayerConfig.split_context_level``: the caller passes the
     cumulative history block as ``user_body`` under ``"medium"`` /
     ``"full"`` and an empty string under ``"minimal"``.

     The caller (``UnifiedTurnManager``) is responsible for formatting the
     forfeit menu (``5-forfeit_option.j2``) and passing it in as
     ``menu_text``.

     Variables:
       user_body       : optional session context (history block); empty
                         string safe.
       menu_text       : str — pre-rendered forfeit menu block.
       forfeit_allowed : bool — gates the CHOICE/REASON schema.
       confidence_block: str|None — pre-rendered "YOUR ASSESSMENT (a
                         moment ago):" block from the confidence call
                         (``build_confidence_block``). Undefined / None
                         renders nothing, so every legacy render is
                         byte-identical.
       always_decide   : bool — ``ForfeitLayerConfig.always_decide``
                         (2026-09-07). Read ONLY when ``forfeit_allowed``
                         is false, where it swaps the framing sentence
                         for one that names no exit: the whole point of
                         the blocked cell under this flag is that the
                         agent is never told an exit exists, and
                         "whether to continue or forfeit" would tell it.
                         Undefined / false keeps the legacy sentence in
                         both branches, so every render before this date
                         — the Cell 2 / Cell 4 characterization
                         snapshots included — is byte-identical. The
                         response-format block below already collapses
                         to a fixed ``CHOICE: CONTINUE`` with no REASON
                         line whenever forfeit is blocked; that part is
                         unchanged and needs no flag.

     2026-09-10, prompt revision v2 (supervisor voice). No "===" marker;
     "LABEL: sentence". "decide whether to continue or forfeit" ->
     "decide: CONTINUE or FORFEIT" (the two words the CHOICE line wants,
     in the case it wants them). The response-format lead collapses to
     "ANSWER FORMAT: ..." (audit L5); the blocked branch says "one line",
     because that branch renders one. The blocked branch's framing
     sentence and the REASON description are untouched.
-#}
{%- if user_body -%}
{{ user_body }}

{% endif -%}
{%- if confidence_block -%}
{{ confidence_block }}

{% endif -%}
{% if forfeit_allowed or not always_decide -%}
A new round is about to begin. Before it is shown to you, decide: CONTINUE or FORFEIT.
{%- else -%}
A new round is about to begin. Before it is shown to you, take stock of where this session stands, then confirm that you are playing this round.
{%- endif %}

{{ menu_text }}

{% if forfeit_allowed %}ANSWER FORMAT: one line per field, in this order.
CHOICE: <CONTINUE or FORFEIT>
REASON: <required only if CHOICE is FORFEIT — a single digit 1, 2, or 3 as listed in the menu>
{% else %}ANSWER FORMAT: one line.
CHOICE: CONTINUE
{% endif %}
